# Federated app CSS

Shell and this kit use **Tailwind CSS v3.4** with the app root class `gf-federated-app`.

- Import `src/index.css` from `App.tsx` so styles ship with `remoteEntry.js`.
- Wrap UI in `FederatedAppRoot`.
- Keep `important: '.gf-federated-app'` and `corePlugins.preflight: false` in `tailwind.config.js`. Never re-enable preflight in the federated build — it resets Shell chrome. The kit's scoped reset in `src/index.css` is required for standalone `npm run dev`.
- Brand colour: `theme.primaryColor` on the manifest (applied in `FederatedAppRoot`). Header logos: `theme.logoUrl` (absolute https). Production builds: Vite `base: './'`.

If the app uses a **different** CSS framework (Bootstrap, MUI global CSS, etc.):

- Do not import that CSS globally.
- Use `FederatedStyleRoot` with `import './vendor.css?inline'` so styles apply inside Shadow DOM only.
- Portal modals to a node inside that shadow root, not `document.body`.

Full guide: `docs/css-and-styling.md`. Public: https://docs.groundfloor.cloud/docs/apps/shell/styling. MCP: `docs_get` id `css-and-styling`.
